---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro'

const title = 'Specimen'
---

<PageLayout title={title} pathname="/dress.css/specimen/">
	<h1>{title}</h1>

	<hr />

	<p>
		This Specimen is styled like a fashion portfolio: the copy flows like fabric,
		and every component shows how <strong>dress.css</strong> handles elegance.
		Imagine the sample garment spinning on a dress form, the CSS seams invisible
		but precise.
	</p>

	<p>
		We treat typography like silk pleats, layout widths like hemlines, and colour
		tokens like dye baths. Scroll for a tour of silhouettes, trend notes, and the
		best fitting appointments in town.
	</p>

	<h2>Lookbook</h2>
	<p>
		Each garment below references a CSS token or component. Use
		<a href="#fit-notes">fit notes</a> for production-ready measurements or jump
		to <a href="#atelier">atelier scheduling</a> to book a fitting.
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Café Shift Dress</strong> — set in <code>--dress-sec</code> teal with
			contrast piping to showcase link colours.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Gallery Gown</strong> — bias-cut in midnight silk, buttons inherit
			<code>--dress-bt-1</code> so hover states glow.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Traveller’s Trench</strong> — ponte knit with expandable pockets and
			a <kbd>double-breasted</kbd> closure, perfect for long flights.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<blockquote>
		<p>
			“Great dresses, like great stylesheets, move effortlessly between
			moments.”<br /><br />— Studio mantra
		</p>
	</blockquote>

	<h2 id="fit-notes">Fit notes & Materials</h2>
	<dl>
		<dt>Corset waist</dt>
		<dd>Supported with cotton sateen coutil, top-stitched with 3 mm spacing.</dd>
		<dt>Sleeve cap</dt>
		<dd>Light organza roll keeps the shoulder sculpted without bulk.</dd>
		<dt>Skirt lining</dt>
		<dd>Breathable cupro, bias bound in matching <mark>accent</mark> tape.</dd>
	</dl>

	<figure>
		<img src="/dress.css/triangles.svg" alt="Mood board triangles" />
		<figcaption>
			The triangles echo godet inserts that give the skirt its fluid swish.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>

	<h2 id="atelier">Atelier schedule</h2>
	<p>
		All appointments take place in the eighth-floor studio. Steam presses are
		warmed at dawn, and the playlist mixes city ambience with runway drums.
	</p>

	<details>
		<summary>⚠️ Fitting checklist</summary>
		<ul>
			<li>Bring the heels and garments you plan to wear.</li>
			<li>Hydrate fabrics with a light mist before final pressing.</li>
			<li>
				Confirm seam allowances (<em>1.5 cm</em> standard) before signing off
				on the toile.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</details>

	<table>
		<caption>Sample pairings</caption>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Look</th>
				<th>Fabric</th>
				<th>Style notes</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Day promenade</td>
				<td>Ivory poplin</td>
				<td>Hidden placket, generous pockets</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Moonlit reception</td>
				<td>Onyx silk</td>
				<td>Beaded straps, puddle hem</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Weekend escape</td>
				<td>Sage ponte knit</td>
				<td>Convertible collar, snap closures</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h3>Styling checklist</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Press seams toward the back to keep the waistline smooth.</li>
		<li>
			Layer delicate jewelry over high necklines to balance the silhouette.
		</li>
		<li>
			Finish hems with blind stitches so the fabric appears to float.
		</li>
	</ol>

	<aside>
		<h4>Texture study</h4>
		<p>
			Combine matte belts with glossy bodices to emphasise <strong>contrast</strong>.
			A single pearl button can act as the <code>call-to-action</code> of an
			outfit.
		</p>
	</aside>

	<h2>Book a fitting</h2>
	<p>
		We host small atelier sessions across London, Montréal, and Kyoto. Add your
		preferences below—this demonstration form embraces every element in the
		toolkit.
	</p>

	<p>
		<mark><strong>Note</strong></mark> This form is only a sample. The submit
		button activates when each field is complete.
	</p>

	<form id="signup" method="post" data-nosubmit>
		<label>
			<span
				>Full Name <small><mark><strong>required</strong></mark></small></span
			>
			<input type="text" placeholder="Given Name" required />
			<input type="text" placeholder="Family Name" required />
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Email <small><mark><strong>required</strong></mark></small></span>
			<input type="email" placeholder="name@example.com" required />
			<small>We’ll send lookbook updates and tailoring reminders.</small>
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Preferred studio</span>
			<select>
				<option>London</option>
				<option>Montréal</option>
				<option>Kyoto</option>
				<option>New York</option>
				<option>Other</option>
			</select>
		</label>

		<fieldset>
			<legend>Session type</legend>
			<label>
				<input type="checkbox" name="session" value="fitting" />
				<span>Private fitting</span>
			</label>
			<label>
				<input type="checkbox" name="session" value="workshop" />
				<span>Pattern workshop</span>
			</label>
			<label>
				<input type="checkbox" name="session" value="preview" />
				<span>Runway preview</span>
			</label>
		</fieldset>

		<fieldset>
			<legend>Contact format</legend>
			<label>
				<input type="radio" name="format" value="html" required />
				<span>Email newsletter</span>
			</label>
			<label>
				<input type="radio" name="format" value="sms" />
				<span>SMS reminder</span>
			</label>
			<label>
				<input type="radio" name="format" value="call" />
				<span>Phone call with stylist</span>
			</label>
		</fieldset>

		<label>
			<span>Colour inspiration</span>
			<input type="color" value="#6699ff" />
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Outfit mood</span>
			<input type="range" min="0" max="10" value="7" />
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Reference image</span>
			<input type="file" />
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Appointment date</span>
			<input type="date" />
		</label>

		<label>
			<span>Preferred fitting time</span>
			<input type="time" value="13:30" />
		</label>

		<menu>
			<li><button type="submit">Reserve</button></li>
			<li><button type="reset">Reset</button></li>
		</menu>
	</form>
</PageLayout>
